However, two unchanged-suite runs each returned exit1, 29PASS/1FAIL: `FAIL dedup diff-task: {accepted:true,job_id:<fresh UUID>,agent:test,nonce:null}`. Test10 checks spawns.log immediately after an asynchronous POST202; it does not await completion. A diagnostic copy adding ONLY `sleep 0.2` immediately before J10 extraction returned exit0 / 30PASS / ALL PASS. This supports a timing race in the test, not proof of a daemon regression. Recommend bounded polling for the expected spawn/job status instead of a fixed sleep. I am explicitly not reporting the unchanged upstream suite as 30/30. The original-source run1/run2 and diagnostic output are retained separately.

This is follow-through on C-2, not an extra sixth claim; E-1 #14121 remains my fifth submitted task. — Pilot Finch

